    <bpmn:process id="W_W1618" name="W1618. Regulatory Incident Reporting &amp; Government Notification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Product safety incident requiring government notification (customer injury, environmental release, regulatory violation)
Frequency: Rare (~1–3 incidents/year)
Volume: Low frequency, high regulatory impact
Owner: Compliance Officer
Participants: Compliance Officer, Legal Counsel, VP Merchandising, Quality Manager
Source: workflow W1618 — Regulatory Incident Reporting &amp; Government Notification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1618_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1618_Lane1" name="Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1618_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1618_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1618_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1618_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1618_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1618_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1618_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1618_Start3" name="Product safety incident requiring government notification (customer injury, environmental…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1618_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1618_Task4" name="Incident reported: (a) customer injury in-store or from product use, (b)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Incident reported: (a) customer injury in-store or from product use, (b) environmental release (chemical spill at DC or store), (c) regulatory inspection finding (BIR, DENR, DOLE, DTI), (d) product safety complaint with injury allegation
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal / CEO
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1618_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1618_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1618_Task5" name="Compliance Officer classifies incident per reporting requirement: (a) DTI —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Compliance Officer classifies incident per reporting requirement: (a) DTI — consumer product safety incident (RA 7394), (b) DENR — hazardous material release (RA 6969 and its IRR), (c) FDA — if applicable product categories, (d) DOLE — workplace safety incident (if employee injured), (e) BIR — tax/compliance violation finding, (f) LGU — local ordinance violation
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1618_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1618_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1618_Task6" name="Prepare regulatory notification: (a) incident description with factual details…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Prepare regulatory notification: (a) incident description with factual details (no admission of liability), (b) product identification (SKU, lot/batch, vendor), (c) actions taken (product removal, customer notification, remediation), (d) timeline of events, (e) Legal Counsel reviews before submission
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1618_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1618_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1618_Task7" name="Submit notification to appropriate agency within required timeline (DTI: within…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Submit notification to appropriate agency within required timeline (DTI: within 48 hours; DENR: within 24 hours for significant release; DOLE: within 48 hours for serious workplace incident)
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1618_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1618_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1618_Task8" name="Respond to government follow-up: (a) provide additional information as…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Respond to government follow-up: (a) provide additional information as requested, (b) facilitate government inspection if directed, (c) implement corrective actions ordered by agency, (d) Legal Counsel manages any formal investigation or enforcement proceedings
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1618_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1618_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1618_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1618_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1618_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-336 (ensure controlled execution — Product Recall &amp; Safety Compliance (PA-31.3).) | - operational: Compliance Officer review and approval gate
Owner: Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1618_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1618_Annotation10" targetRef="W1618_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1618_Flow12" sourceRef="W1618_Start3" targetRef="W1618_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1618_Flow13" sourceRef="W1618_Task4" targetRef="W1618_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1618_Flow14" sourceRef="W1618_Task5" targetRef="W1618_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1618_Flow15" sourceRef="W1618_Task6" targetRef="W1618_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1618_Flow16" sourceRef="W1618_Task7" targetRef="W1618_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1618_Flow17" sourceRef="W1618_Task8" targetRef="W1618_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1618_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1618_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1618">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Task4_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Task4"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Start3_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Start3"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1618_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1618_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="290" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1618_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1618_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1618_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1618_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1618_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1618_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1618_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1618_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="290" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1619" name="W1619. Product Safety Complaint Triage &amp; Escalation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer complaint involving product safety concern (injury, fire, electrical shock, chemical exposure, structural failure)
Frequency: ~20–40 safety complaints/month across all channels
Volume: ~250–500 per year; most resolved at Tier 1; ~5–10 escalated to full safety investigation
Owner: Customer Service Manager
Participants: Customer Service Agent, Customer Service Manager, Quality Manager, Compliance Officer, Legal Counsel
Source: workflow W1619 — Product Safety Complaint Triage &amp; Escalation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1619_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1619_Lane1" name="Customer Service Agent">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1619_Lane2" name="Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1619_Lane3" name="Quality Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1619_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1619_Start5" name="Customer complaint involving product safety concern (injury, fire, electrical shock…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1619_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1619_Task6" name="Critical">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Service Agent receives safety complaint via phone, email, in-store, or social media: (a) records complaint details (customer info, product details, incident description, photos if available, injury/property damage details), (b) classifies severity: (i) Critical — injury requiring medical attention, fire, structural collapse, (ii) High — near-miss with injury potential, significant property damage risk, (iii) Medium — product malfunction without immediate safety risk, (iv) Low — quality issue not safety-related (route to standard complaint handling)
Responsible (R): Customer Service Agent
Accountable (A): Customer Service Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1619_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1619_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1619_Task7" name="Critical severity">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Critical severity: immediate escalation to Customer Service Manager and Compliance Officer; product images and incident details forwarded within 1 hour; customer advised to stop using product and offered immediate refund/replacement
Responsible (R): Customer Service Agent / Customer Service Manager
Accountable (A): Compliance Officer
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1619_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1619_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1619_Task8" name="Compliance Officer reviews Critical/High complaints within 4 hours: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Compliance Officer reviews Critical/High complaints within 4 hours: (a) determines if complaint is isolated or part of a pattern (searches complaint database for similar reports on same SKU/lot), (b) if pattern detected (2+ similar complaints within 30 days): initiates recall assessment per W1615, (c) if isolated: initiates product investigation — request customer return the product for Quality Manager inspection
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 30 min/complaint</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1619_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1619_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1619_Task9" name="Quality Manager inspects returned product: (a) visual and functional…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quality Manager inspects returned product: (a) visual and functional examination, (b) comparison to specification and control sample, (c) root cause hypothesis (manufacturing defect, misuse, installation error, design flaw), (d) if needed: sends to external testing laboratory for material/functional analysis
Responsible (R): Quality Manager
Accountable (A): Compliance Officer
Duration: 1–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1619_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1619_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1619_Task10" name="Product defect confirmed">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Investigation conclusion: (a) Product defect confirmed: route to VCAR (W1610) and potential recall (W1615), (b) Customer misuse/installation error: customer education; no product action; consider updating product instructions or warning labels, (c) Inconclusive: monitor for additional complaints; keep case open for 90 days
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer / Quality Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1619_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1619_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1619_Task11" name="Monthly: Compliance Officer reviews all safety complaint data — trend analysis…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly: Compliance Officer reviews all safety complaint data — trend analysis by category, vendor, and complaint type; reports to Quality Manager and Category Managers for proactive quality improvement
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1619_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1619_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1619_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1619_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
