    <bpmn:process id="W_W5503" name="W5503. Restricted-Substance &amp; Chemical-Content Product Compliance — Lead-in-Paint (DENR CCO), Formaldehyde Emission &amp; VOC Limits" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Program establishment and annual RSL refresh; (b) new in-scope SKU or vendor onboarding (VS-03.1 / W564 NPI); (c) arrival of an import lot of paint, coatings, or engineered-wood panels; (d) regulatory change (DENR CCO amendment, DTI-BPS standard update, FDA/DOH advisory); (e) failed verification test, vendor reformulation notice, or product-safety complaint (W1619)
Frequency: Continuous item-creation and goods-receipt gates; ~250–340 new-SKU/vendor declarations per year; ~100–150 in-scope import lot-CoA verifications per month; ~10–15 verification tests per month; RSL review annual plus event-driven
Volume: ~4,200–4,700 in-scope SKUs of the 35,000 active catalog — Paint &amp; Finishes ~2,800; engineered-wood panels (plywood/MDF/veneer inside Lumber &amp; Building Materials) ~1,000; adhesives, grout and sealants (inside Tiles &amp; Flooring) ~400–900 — sourced from ~150–180 of the ~800–1,000 active vendors; ~40% of the 400–600 import TEUs/month carry in-scope goods, so ~100–150 TEU lots per month need lot-level chemical evidence
Owner: Quality Manager
Participants: Compliance Officer, Category Manager (Paint / Lumber &amp; Building Materials), Buyer, Imports &amp; Customs Coordinator (VS-122), DC Quality Inspector (PA-31.1), Merchandising Operations &amp; Master Data (VS-29), Legal &amp; Compliance, Private Brand team (VS-41), third-party testing laboratory
Source: workflow W5503 — Restricted-Substance &amp; Chemical-Content Product Compliance — Lead-in-Paint (DENR CCO), Formaldehyde Emission &amp; VOC Limits</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5503_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5503_Lane1" name="Quality Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5503_Lane2" name="Merchandising Ops &amp; Master Data">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5503_Lane3" name="DC Quality Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5503_Lane4" name="Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5503_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5503_Start6" name="(a) Program establishment and annual RSL refresh; (b) new in-scope SKU or vendor…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task7" name="RSL adoption and maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: RSL adoption and maintenance: Quality Manager maintains the BuildRight Restricted Substance List covering (a) lead and lead compounds — 90 ppm total lead in paints per DENR CCO 2013-24, with RA 6969 lead-in-consumer-products restrictions as the wider frame; (b) formaldehyde release limits for wood-based panels (E1/E0 emission classes per the PNS/ISO 12460-series methods as invoked in import specs); (c) VOC content limits for architectural coatings per PNS paint standards and referenced international limits; (d) an import watch-list layer (heavy metals in colorants, phthalates in PVC fittings and sealants) benchmarked to recognized international RSLs since ~40% of in-scope goods are imported; reviewed annually and on every DENR EMB / DTI-BPS / FDA issuance; RSL version mapped to an item-master compliance attribute by category
Responsible (R): Quality Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3–5 days initial; 2–3 days/year refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task8" name="Vendor declaration and evidence">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor declaration and evidence: every in-scope vendor — new per VS-03.1, existing at annual refresh — signs a restricted-substance declaration and supplies third-party test reports per material family (lead content for paint and colorant SKUs; formaldehyde-emission class for panel SKUs; VOC content for coatings), renewed on any reformulation, raw-material source change, or factory relocation; private-brand vendors (VS-41) are contractually bound to the RSL with audit rights; evidence tracked on the vendor record per W1612
Responsible (R): Quality Manager / Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30–45 min per declaration</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task9" name="Item-master gate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Item-master gate: a new in-scope SKU cannot be activated without RSL attributes — scope flag, applicable limits, certificate reference and expiry; the NPI checklist (W564) carries the chemical-compliance sign-off; Merchandising Operations &amp; Master Data maintain the flags (VS-29)
Responsible (R): Merchandising Ops &amp; Master Data
Accountable (A): Quality Manager
Duration: 10 min/SKU (gate check)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task10" name="Import lot evidence at goods receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Import lot evidence at goods receipt: for import lots of paint, coatings and panels, the lot-level CoA (lead content or formaldehyde class per lot) is verified against PO terms at pre-shipment verification (W1613), checked at import PDI (W1602), and attached at goods receipt (W1600); a missing or failing CoA triggers a lot hold (W1603) pending verification testing; local and DSD purchases verify the annual certificate plus risk-based lot sampling
Responsible (R): DC Quality Inspector / Imports Coordinator
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min/lot</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task11" name="Verification testing program">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Verification testing program: risk-based sampling of ~10–15 samples/month at DENR-accredited or BPS-recognized laboratories — budget decorative-paint brands, budget plywood, newly onboarded vendors, reformulations, complaint-driven pulls (W1619) and regulatory-alert pulls; a failure triggers vendor CAPA (W1610), lot quarantine (W1603), scorecard impact (W1608) and re-test of the vendor&#x27;s next three lots
Responsible (R): Quality Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–4 hrs/month coordination; 30–60 days lab turnaround</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task12" name="Non-compliant lot and SKU handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Non-compliant lot and SKU handling: stop-sale/hold flag raised on affected lots and SKUs chain-wide (DC quarantine bin per W1603; store pull-from-sale list), disposition decided (RTV, lawful rework, or DENR-compliant disposal per W82/W5347); if sold units exist, consumer-exposure assessment routes to recall assessment W1615 / VS-89; government notification per W1618 where required (DENR EMB, DTI-BPS, FDA); Legal &amp; Compliance (VS-100) pursues contractual recovery
Responsible (R): Quality Manager / Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): Compliance Officer
Duration: 4–8 hrs per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task13" name="Regulatory monitoring and reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Regulatory monitoring and reporting: quarterly regulatory-intelligence review with VS-22 and the VS-166 register for DENR EMB CCO amendments, DTI-BPS PNS updates and FDA/DOH advisories; respond to DENR market-surveillance findings within stated deadlines; report RSL compliance KPIs into VS-25 sourcing disclosures and VS-21 audit evidence
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 2 hrs/quarter + event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5503_Task14" name="Analytics and program review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Analytics and program review: quarterly review of declaration coverage %, CoA completeness % at goods receipt, test pass rate by category and vendor, blocked-lot value, and CAPA closure time; feeds the vendor scorecard (W1608 / VS-67) and the assortment risk view for Category Managers
Responsible (R): Quality Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hrs/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5503_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5503_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5503_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5503_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-336 (ensure controlled execution — Product Recall &amp; Safety Compliance (PA-31.3).) | - CTL-336 (ensure controlled execution — Product Recall &amp; Safety Compliance (PA-31.3).) | - operational: lot-CoA match verified before lot release; stop-sale flag confirmed before any disposition
Owner: Quality Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5503_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5503_Annotation16" targetRef="W5503_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
